text:
amanda: Quick: AcmeHealth POC requirements — single websocket multiplexing, streaming SSE, in-stream function/tool calls, strict JSON schema output, EU data residency, and SSO/KMS for Private. They also want a 1-week ballpark for 500 QPS. Need runbook + legal blurb + tiny SDK snippet before tomorrow.

raj: We support multiplexing via session_id per logical stream. Hosted may rebalance; Dedicated with sticky routing recommended for stable tool-call ordering.

ben: Short answers: 1) Schema enforcement should be done client-side; use our optional "schema_hints" to reduce parse failures. 2) Tool calls are emitted as structured events; handler must reply with a JSON string. 3) Ephemeral creds supported (default rotation 15m).

amanda: Drop a minimal Node + curl snippet we can send.

raj: Node snippet:
```js
const WebSocket = require('ws');
const ws = new WebSocket(process.env.POC_WS_URL);
ws.on('open', () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'open', session_id: 's1', model: 'rwd-stream' }));
});
ws.on('message', raw => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(raw);
  if (msg.type === 'token') console.log(msg.session_id, msg.token);
  if (msg.type === 'tool_call') {
    const result = { ok: true, patient: { id: msg.args.id } };
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'tool_response', session_id: msg.session_id, call_id: msg.call_id, result: JSON.stringify(result) }));
  }
});
```
Curl handshake:
curl -X POST "https://api.redwood.ai/handshake" -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"session_id":"s1","schema_hints":{"patient":{"id":"string"}}}'
// returns {"ws_url":"wss://...","expires_in":900}

sarah: Legal blurb draft: "Runtime keeps transient KV/cache data in-memory for session duration and does not persist raw prompt/response tokens to disk in Dedicated or Private by default. Customers may enable logging; exported logs follow retention policy. Customer-managed KMS is used for at-rest encryption; key rotation follows customer policy. Audit records for admin/provisioning events are available via Console per contract."

ben: Concise POC runbook:
1) Exchange IdP metadata and KMS ARN.
2) We provision EU Dedicated test pool (2-3 days) or Private on-prem (2-3 weeks).
3) POST /handshake -> ws_url + token.
4) Open websocket, multiplex sessions with session_id, include schema_hints.
5) Respond to tool_call events with tool_response JSON; ensure idempotence.
6) Post-demo rotate ephemeral creds via /rotate-ephemeral.

amanda: Pricing ballpark for 500 QPS sustained for 1 week (EU Dedicated test)?

ben: Ballpark: ~40-50M tokens/day. One-week Dedicated test (reserved pool + support + EU infra) estimate $25k-$45k. Monthly reserved drops unit cost significantly; will follow up with formal quote.

raj: Note: if they need strict ordering and exactly-once semantics, use Dedicated with sticky sessions and make tool handlers idempotent. Hosted is fine for demo but may route across pods under load.

